### 15.7 Permission Inheritance

**Default**: **Inheritable** - Step permissions inherit from workflow, workflow from agent

**Rationale**:
- Less verbose YAML (no permission repetition)
- Hierarchical control
- Override only when needed

**Inheritance Rules**:
```yaml
workflow:
  permissions:
    agent: "read-only"  # All steps inherit read-only
  - step: Safe analysis
    # Inherits read-only automatically
  - step: Write report
    permissions:
      agent: "write"  # Override to enable writing
```

### 15.8 Profiling and Metrics

**Level**: **Yes, very detailed metrics**

**Metrics to Collect**:
- **Timing Metrics**:
  - Time to respond (first token)
  - Thinking time (before tool call)
  - Tool execution time (each tool)
  - Loop iteration time
  - Total workflow time

- **LLM Metrics**:
  - Token I/O counts (input tokens, output tokens)
  - Tokens per second
  - Context window usage
  - Memory usage (average)
  - Memory usage at specified intervals (user-configurable)

- **Execution Metrics**:
  - Line-item level logging for each operation
  - Parallel execution support
  - Tool usage frequency
  - Success/failure rates

- **Model Settings**:
  - Model name and version
  - Backend (Vulkan, CUDA, Metal)
  - Context size
  - Temperature, top-k, top-p

- **I/O Logging**:
  - Input prompt IO for different stages
  - Output variable references for stage results

- **Advanced Features**:
  - Parallel execution tracking
  - Smart graceful degradation when local system overwhelmed
  - Orchestration strategies for local context management

